00:16:34.770 --> 00:16:37.520
The last <i>dojo</i>  listed on Sparna's list.

00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:38.180
Correct Sir.

00:16:38.180 --> 00:16:39.240
What's written there?

00:16:39.240 --> 00:16:42.880
Why do Japanese have Katakana, Hiragana, and Kanji as their alphabets?

00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:44.700
I can't read a single Kanji!

00:16:44.700 --> 00:16:45.320
Roger!

00:16:45.320 --> 00:16:47.470
I think it's Haku, Zan and Ryou.

00:16:47.470 --> 00:16:48.790
Haku Zan?

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:51.510
Why does those words sound familiar?

00:16:51.510 --> 00:16:52.570
Oh well.

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:53.240
Let's go!

00:16:54.670 --> 00:16:55.850
Visitors?

00:17:00.760 --> 00:17:02.620
This feels great.

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:06.490
Honoka, do you come here everyday?

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:07.990
Usually.

00:17:07.990 --> 00:17:11.470
He listens to anything that I say whenever he loses.

00:17:11.470 --> 00:17:12.870
Very convenient.

00:17:12.870 --> 00:17:15.750
Is your little sister some demon or what?

00:17:15.750 --> 00:17:18.990
I think you should give up already, Tanimoto-kun.

00:17:18.990 --> 00:17:20.760
She's really strong.

00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:22.780
I won't give up.

00:17:23.130 --> 00:17:24.780
No matter what.

00:17:25.180 --> 00:17:28.150
You really hate losing don’t you, Natsu?

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:30.990
I promised that person before,

00:17:30.990 --> 00:17:32.890
that I would never lose.

00:17:33.670 --> 00:17:35.400
I'm sorry,

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:39.830
I don't think... I'll be able to make it.

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:43.420
Onii-chan, please don't lose, okay?

00:17:45.610 --> 00:17:46.900
That's weird.

00:17:46.900 --> 00:17:49.430
<i>His promise to his late sister, huh?</i>

00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:53.390
But, isn't doing it over and over until you win a bit too rough?

00:17:53.390 --> 00:17:54.280
Shut up!

00:17:54.280 --> 00:17:56.830
Don't question my core principles!

00:17:56.830 --> 00:17:58.390
Even your voice is shaky, you know?

00:17:58.530 --> 00:17:59.180
<i>I see.</i>

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:02.800
<i>He's protecting the promise that he made a long time ago.</i>

00:18:02.800 --> 00:18:05.340
<i>That explains why he's so determined to win no matter what.</i>

00:18:05.340 --> 00:18:07.290
<i>This guy sure is amazing.</i>

00:18:07.870 --> 00:18:09.540
Are you okay with this?

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:10.180
Huh?

00:18:10.510 --> 00:18:11.830
You promised too, right?

00:18:11.830 --> 00:18:13.570
That you would protect someone.

00:18:13.990 --> 00:18:16.640
So is it really okay for you to be slacking off here?

00:18:19.090 --> 00:18:20.070
<i>Bullseye.</i>

00:18:21.920 --> 00:18:23.150
But you know,

00:18:23.150 --> 00:18:28.500
I already promised to cook Apachai hamburgers as long as he keeps his mouth shut about this place,

00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:31.290
and if I die so soon, I can't really protect her anyway.

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:32.800
That's right!

00:18:32.800 --> 00:18:35.690
Onii-chan's body is more important than Big Boobs!

00:18:35.910 --> 00:18:38.170
<i>Damn, just a little more and he would have left.</i>

00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:43.800
<i>Though it's a a good probability that the guy may be strengthening himself while I'm slacking off here.</i>

00:18:44.730 --> 00:18:47.190
<i>When I think about that, I grow more and more impatient.</i>

00:18:47.800 --> 00:18:49.530
Oh, so it's Hakuzanryou.

00:18:49.530 --> 00:18:51.190
It looks the most worn down compared to others.

00:18:51.190 --> 00:18:52.610
Yes, Commander.

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:55.570
But Japanese <i>dojos</i>  sure are weak.

00:18:55.570 --> 00:18:56.260
Wrong.

00:18:56.260 --> 00:18:57.920
It's because we are strong!

00:18:57.920 --> 00:18:58.740
Let's go!

00:18:58.740 --> 00:18:59.500
Yes sir!

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:06.450
Don't move, the place is booby-trapped!

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:18.050
<i>There should be no traps on the roof.</i>

00:19:18.050 --> 00:19:19.440
<i>We'll split into three groups.</i>

00:19:19.440 --> 00:19:22.000
<i>One group will scout the offensive capability of the enemy,</i>

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:24.210
<i>by heading for the highest structure.</i>

00:19:25.970 --> 00:19:29.640
<i>It seems that Japan has one formidable  </i>dojo<i> after all.</i>

00:19:29.640 --> 00:19:30.480
<i>However,</i>

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:32.230
